Local modifications:
- Extract only the HD1910 M6 equations into pure PyTorch functions.
- Add an immutable, validated parameter schema and explicit actuator alias.
- Avoid the upstream BAM/mjlab dependency and initialization machinery.
- Retain fitted q_offset and command_delay as metadata without applying them.
- Keep viscous damping and friction randomization outside the dry-friction budget.
- Integrate with mjlab 1.6 using independent per-world friction model fields.
- Apply an explicit motor/joint torque cap and seed native friction constraints.
- Invalidate preceding-solve loads on partial reset; let mjlab apply delay once.
- Apply optional dry-friction scaling once and resample only selected resets.
- Recover direct and projected external loads from the preceding smooth force.
- Mark preceding-solve loads valid in post-step update, not control writes.

The M6 quadratic term follows pinned bam/model.py, the scalar identification
model: it is enabled only for opposite torque signs, and only for unequal
absolute motor/load magnitudes. This corrects the pinned bam/mjlab.py port,
which omits the sign gate and takes its backdrive branch for equal magnitudes.

Bundled parameter JSON is an unmodified manufacturer's public 7.4 V fit.
It is not a measurement or calibration of the HT Microduck robot. See
params/README.md for source, checksum and identification metadata limitations.
